{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/Html/Printer.html#Lean.Html.render\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Html</span>.<span class=\"name\">render</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Html/Basic.html#Lean.Html\">Html</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Renders into a string to be consumed by browsers.\nThe input's structure is respected as much as possible:\n\n* No whitespace is added or removed.\n\n* Tag names are not escaped.\n\nThe output uses [HTML5 syntax](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/syntax.html).\nIt is not compatible with [XML syntax for HTML](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/xhtml.html).\n\n# Details of the output syntax\n\nWe make the following XML-compatible choices:\n\n* Void elements with `isEmpty` children are rendered as self-closing tags.\n\n  * Void elements with non-`isEmpty` children are rendered like normal elements.\n    Such elements are forbidden by the HTML spec.\n\n* Attribute values are always double-quoted.\n\nAnd the following incompatible choices:\n\n* Attributes with empty values are [minimized](https://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/#h-4.5). ","docLink":"./Lean/Data/Html/Printer.html#Lean.Html.render","kind":"def","line":76,"name":"Lean.Html.render","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Data/Html/Printer.lean#L76-L146"}}],"imports":["Init.Data.String.Search","Lean.Data.Html.Basic","Lean.Data.Html.Spec"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Data.Html.Printer"}